<title>FRANCE: Machinery tops Paris '96 air exports to NAmerica.</title>
<headline>Machinery tops Paris '96 air exports to NAmerica.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Machinery, motors, equipment and parts was the leading category of goods exported to North America from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in 1996, French Ministry of Transport (MoT) figures showed.</p>
<p>The top ten category of goods exported from the Paris</p>
<p>airports to North America in 1996 in tonnes with percentage</p>
<p>change from 1995 were:</p>
<p>	  Category		 1996	  Pct change</p>
<p>  1. Machinery, motors	12,292	 down   7.4</p>
<p>equipment &amp; parts</p>
<p>  2. Perfumes		    4,145	 up     5.5</p>
<p>  3. Assorted		    3,692	 up    13.8</p>
<p>manufactured goods</p>
<p>  4. Travel goods/garments   2,187	 down   1.4</p>
<p>/hosiery/footwear</p>
<p>  5. Printed matter	    1,877	 down  18.6</p>
<p>  6. Vehicles/transport	1,417	 down 116.9</p>
<p>equipment/parts</p>
<p>  7. Textiles/fabrics	  1,411		 n.a.</p>
<p>  8. Raw plastics		  664	 down  22.6</p>
<p>  9. Assorted chemicals	  415	 up    48.3</p>
<p>materials</p>
<p> 10. Medicines/		   410	  up    50.7</p>
<p>pharmaceuticals.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
